AI Security Copilot™ Multi-Tenant Isolation & Context-Aware Intelligence

The QGuard Helix AI Security Copilot™ must be designed as a strictly tenant-isolated, context-aware AI assistant. It must only access and analyze data that belongs to the currently authenticated user and their organization. Under no circumstances should the AI have visibility into or access data belonging to any other tenant, customer, organization, or user.

The AI must function as a secure enterprise assistant that provides accurate, personalized, and evidence-based recommendations using only the authenticated tenant's data and permissions.

Multi-Tenant Security Requirements

Implement a zero cross-tenant architecture where every AI request is scoped to the authenticated tenant.

Each AI request must automatically inherit:

Tenant ID
Organization ID
User ID
Workspace ID (if applicable)
User Role (RBAC)
Assigned Permissions
Subscription Plan
Current Session Context

Every query, recommendation, and response generated by the AI must be filtered using these identities before accessing any platform data.

The AI must never access, retrieve, cache, reference, or expose information belonging to another customer, organization, or tenant.

